// Oracle question: does `#elif` work at the two levels below the top?
//
// `compiler.inc` gives `#if`/`#else`/`#endif` productions at all three levels
// where regions nest - `TopList` (:7-10), `DataList` (:98-101) and `Sequence`
// (:142-145) - and each level's `PPElse` alternative has a `PPElIf` sibling.
// So the grammar says yes.
//
// It is not yes.  The generated parser aborts on this file: `free(): invalid
// pointer`, SIGABRT, exit 134, with no diagnostic at all.  A top-level
// `#elif` is fine - `preprocessor-condition-reads` uses one - so the defect is
// in the two inner levels only.
//
// K816 supports `#elif` uniformly at all three, which is a strict superset of
// what the original *accepts* and is what makes the imported fixture
// `legacy-k816/syntax-preprocessor-sequence-and-data` compile at all.

data answers {
  #if 0
  0x21
  #elif 1
  0x11
  #endif
}

main {
  a = answers
  return
}
